From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:48:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] perf(web): read H.264 regions that are far apart one by
 one

The decoder read all of a frame's regions back in one call, as their
bounding box. Two small regions in opposite corners of the picture (a
clock, a cursor) made that box the whole picture: 33 MB read and
allocated for a 4K frame to get eight bytes.

When the box holds more than twice what the regions do, each region is
read on its own, straight into its place in the result; regions that are
close together are still read as one box.
